The rule for recover_json_object says the object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text. For the input fence[ A B ], the fence holds two objects, A and B, so the last one inside the fence, B, is scored. For the rewritten text fence[ A B ] C, the fence still holds A and B, and C is after the fence, so the last one inside the fence remains B. Therefore the recovery kernel should be unchanged between the two texts.